  "title": "In Fano trees the dictionary up to distance two is one touching rule",
  "subject": "What the completed screening lemmas prove about the brace dictionary",
  "conclusion": "In spaces built from Fano atoms alone, a line creates at another exactly when it does in the chain of their atoms, and between atoms at most two apart exactly when the receiving line touches its atom's cut toward the removal. So native creation keeps each atom whole and reads every cut in its direction, and only a transfer along longer chains remains before the source rule is a theorem.",
